WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.991
Solar storm.

2
00:00:02.031 --> 00:00:04.499
When the Sun flares up, here's where to
go.

3
00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:10.633
Sometimes, the Sun erupts, and throws out
a burst of high-energy protons.

4
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:15.948
The fastest can reach you in less than an
hour, and they go right through the walls.

5
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:18.040
Far from Earth's magnetic field,

6
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.631
on the way to the Moon or Mars, the risk
is even higher.

7
00:00:22.531 --> 00:00:27.081
Space weather forecasters watch the Sun
around the clock, and send the alert.

8
00:00:27.981 --> 00:00:31.039
When it comes, the crew moves to the most
shielded

9
00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:33.425
spot, surrounded by water and supplies.

10
00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:37.567
The more mass around you, the fewer
particles get through.

11
00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:42.705
You may stay there for hours. Wear your
dosimeter, and wait for the all clear.

12
00:00:43.605 --> 00:00:47.108
A few hours in the shelter can spare you a
large dose.

